></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1055981A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> </non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOIKE KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIDENORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU EISAKU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOIKE, KUNIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, EISAKU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOIKE KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIDENORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU EISAKU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOIKE, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, EISAKU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A generator (20) is connected in parallel with a bypass circuit (31) and a capacitor (22) for storing electric energy from the generator, and the bypass circuit (31) includes a switch (33) that is controlled to turn on and off depending on the voltage across the capacitor (22). Since the input current to the capacitor decreases, the capacitor voltage becomes low, thus preventing overcharge. The waveform of the generated power corresponds to the cycle of the generator rotation, and the rotation of the generator is controlled accurately according to the waveform so that the accurate time indication can be achieved.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un générateur (20) relié en parallèle à un circuit de dérivation (31) et à un condensateur (22) qui stocke l'énergie électrique produite par le générateur. Le circuit de dérivation (31) est équipé d'un commutateur (33) commandé pour être en marche et à l'arrêt en fonction de la tension établie aux bornes du condensateur (22). Etant donné que le courant d'entrée fourni au condensateur diminue, la tension aux bornes du condensateur devient faible, ce qui permet d'éviter les surcharges. La forme d'onde de la puissance engendrée correspond au cycle de rotation du générateur, et ladite rotation est commandée avec précision en fonction de la forme d'onde, moyennant quoi il est possible d'avoir une indication horaire précise.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the 